Split out of #81, whose upstream half is done and released.

Git::Native 0.004 makes fetch and push return a Git::Native::Remote::Result:

    my $r = $remote->fetch(refspecs => [...]);
    $r->updated    # [ { ref, from, to }, ... ]  accepted moves
    $r->rejected   # [ { ref, reason }, ... ]    push rejections

libgit2 still returns 0 from git_remote_fetch/git_remote_push even when the
server rejected individual refs (pre-receive hook, protected ref, non-ff on a
non-forced refspec), so that Result is the only place the rejection shows up.

karr calls fetch/push in App::karr::Git and throws the return value away, so a
push whose refs were all rejected is reported to the user as a successful sync.
The board then diverges from the remote with no signal at all.

Work: consume the Result on both paths. A non-empty ->rejected must fail the
sync with the per-ref reason in the message, not a generic one. Decide what
->updated on fetch is worth: it can tell the reconcile path which refs actually
moved instead of re-reading everything.

Also relevant: karr keeps a git-CLI fallback for remote transport. Whatever
error contract the native path grows here, the CLI path has to match it, or the
failure stays invisible for anyone on the fallback.
Fixed and merged into main; full suite green at 88 files / 566 tests.

Every one of these was reproduced before it was fixed and left a regression test
that was verified to fail against the pre-fix code -- not a test that merely
passes now. Details and what was deliberately NOT fixed are in the merge commit
that names this ticket.
